  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Epifriedelin and the Glucagon receptor, mediated through the Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. This protein is targeted by two distinct compounds: (1S,18R,20S,21S,22S)-6,7,8,11,12,13,21,22-octahydroxy-3,16-dioxo-2,17,19-trioxatetracyclo[16.3.1.0^{4,9}.0^{10,15}]docosa-4(9),5,7,10,12,14-hexaen-20-yl 3,4,5-trihydroxybenzoate and 9-Hydroxy-12-oxo-10-octadecenoic acid. Both of these compounds are predicted to interact with the Glucagon receptor, indicating a possible pathway through which Epifriedelin may influence the receptor's function. The scores from the two paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with the first path having a slightly higher score. The evidence highlights a mechanistic link between Epifriedelin and the Glucagon receptor, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
